{"info":{"author":"lxml dev team","author_email":"lxml@lxml.de","bugtrack_url":null,"classifiers":["Development Status :: 4 - Beta","Intended Audience :: Developers","Intended Audience :: Information Technology","Operating System :: OS Independent","Programming Language :: C","Programming Language :: Cython","Programming Language :: Python :: 3","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.13","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.14","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.15","Programming Language :: Python :: 3.9","Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules","Topic :: Text Processing :: Markup :: HTML","Topic :: Text Processing :: Markup :: XML"],"description":"lxml is a Pythonic, mature binding for the libxml2 and libxslt libraries.\nIt provides safe and convenient access to these libraries using the\nElementTree API.\n\nIt extends the ElementTree API significantly to offer support for XPath,\nRelaxNG, XML Schema, XSLT, C14N and much more.\n\nTo contact the project, go to the `project home page <https://lxml.de/>`_\nor see our bug tracker at https://launchpad.net/lxml\n\nIn case you want to use the current in-development version of lxml,\nyou can get it from the github repository at\nhttps://github.com/lxml/lxml .  Note that this requires Cython to\nbuild the sources, see the build instructions on the project home page.\n\n7.0.0b1 (2026-08-22)\n====================\n\nBugs fixed\n----------\n\n* LP#2143321: A ``NameError`` in ``doctestcompare`` when the doctests are processed\n  by a non-standard module.\n  Original patch by Rahul Kumar.\n\n* GH#492: Failures in ``htmldiff()`` to string-join the diff result are now propagated\n  instead of silently returning an empty result.\n  Patch by Juan Carlos Carvajal B.\n\nOther changes\n-------------\n\n* Built using Cython 3.3.0.\n\n\n","description_content_type":null,"docs_url":null,"download_url":null,"downloads":{"last_day":-1,"last_month":-1,"last_week":-1},"dynamic":["Author","Author-Email","Classifier","Description","Home-Page","License","License-File","Maintainer","Maintainer-Email","Project-Url","Provides-Extra","Requires-Python","Summary"],"home_page":"https://lxml.de/","keywords":null,"license":"BSD-3-Clause","license_expression":null,"license_files":["LICENSE.txt","LICENSES.txt"],"maintainer":"lxml dev team","maintainer_email":"lxml@lxml.de","name":"lxml","package_url":"https://pypi.org/project/lxml/","platform":null,"project_url":"https://pypi.org/project/lxml/","project_urls":{"Bug Tracker":"https://bugs.launchpad.net/lxml","Homepage":"https://lxml.de/","Source":"https://github.com/lxml/lxml"},"provides_extra":["source","cssselect","html5","htmlsoup","html-clean"],"release_url":"https://pypi.org/project/lxml/7.0.0b1/","requires_dist":["cssselect>=0.7; extra == \"cssselect\"","html5lib; extra == \"html5\"","BeautifulSoup4; extra == \"htmlsoup\"","lxml_html_clean; extra == \"html-clean\""],"requires_python":">=3.9","summary":"Powerful and Pythonic XML processing library combining libxml2/libxslt with the ElementTree API.","version":"7.0.0b1","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},"last_serial":40282634,"ownership":{"organization":null,"roles":[{"role":"Owner","user":"faassen"},{"role":"Owner","user":"scoder"}]},"urls":[{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"3f405ca120fec38d91b321057c685c8d4bc75253425e1d8e5c153df17c8e69db"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"49e16c54b834bfd96f14221631d6161c41c68fe34bcb204e299339fd70b9c60a","md5":"4684fae71c6f925b180ff0a03e409df4","sha256":"053858ca4c51d1604d105eb9cd25ee2d00b8aee5ee9cde00768e806036463119"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"lxml-7.0.0b1-cp310-cp310-macosx_10_9_universal2.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"4684fae71c6f925b180ff0a03e409df4","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"cp310","requires_python":">=3.9","size":8920638,"upload_time":"2026-08-22T18:03:14","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-08-22T18:0